#
# STATUS: LIVE, 2026-11-15. The kf3 flag set `win_vm.sh run` loads when it is given no --env-file (and no
# --no-default-flags). Only blank lines, '#' comments and KF3_NAME=digits lines are accepted (win_vm.sh load_env_file).
# A flag already set in the caller's environment wins over this file (an explicit --env-file overrides it as a whole).
#
# Owner, 2026-11-15: "To start windows you do not need an env file. Then the defaults are wrong."
#
# MEASURED, 2026-11-15 (the pc, NVIDIA 580.88 in the guest): `win_vm.sh run` with kf3
# and none of these flags, no guest-driver and no gpu-uuid ended in Windows Code 43 (kf3 log: GSP Running -> Suspending
# -> Halted); the same guest launched with exactly this list, guest-driver=580.65.06 and gpu-uuid=GPU-<VM_UUID> reached
# ConfigManagerErrorCode 0 and nvidia-smi worked. Earlier, MEASURED 2026-10-27 (lease 57882297,
# traces/tur1_20261027/run3_windows/w4_refused_set_no_flags.txt): without flags the guest driver was refused
# GFX_POOL_QUERY_SIZE (0x2080121f) and ended in Code 43.
#
# Why every line is a default and none is a diagnostic (read from the code on 2026-11-15, not measured per flag):
#   * Each *_PROBE flag below (PREEMPT_BIND, DISPLAY_CTRL, ZCULL_BIND, GFX_POOL, SW_RUNLIST, MEMORY_LIST) turns ON a
#     policy link that ANSWERS a guest-driver request (crates/kf-rm: preempt_bind_probe, display_ctrl_probe,
#     gfxpool_probe, ...). "PROBE" is the experiment's status name, not "log only".
#   * The rest enable relays and display behaviour the driver needs (channel passthrough, the kernel GR/CE relay,
#     deferred API, async preempt, SDR colour, the LUT mirror).
#   * INFERRED, not measured: that every one of the 19 is NEEDED. Nobody has bisected the list; the whole set is the
#     recorded "Code 0" set (traces/sweep_windows_20261021/p19.flags, branch claude/bw4-b1n-20261024) and the CI
#     Windows gate's set. Shrinking it needs a boot per candidate flag.
#   * KF3_DISPLAY_CAPS_PROBE is read by nothing on `next` (crates/ and qemu/ grepped 2026-11-15; the page it served was
#     removed, crates/kf-qemu/src/display.rs). It is kept so this list stays equal to the gate's recorded set; a
#     later change may drop it from both files.
#
# NOT here, on purpose (diagnostics stay opt-in): KF3_RPC_TRACE (log only; `run` sets it to 1 itself, see
# --no-rpc-trace), WINVM_TRACE / KF3_BAR0_READ_TRACE, KF3_DISPLAY_*_TRACE, KF3_MAPLOG, KF3_TCENSUS and the other
# trace/census flags. The lazy-observe / lifecycle settings of the owner's 2026-10-26 rule are not here either: whether
# they are defaults was not checked.
#
# kf3_flags.sample.env (the name the CI gates and the propimage bundle still pass) carries the SAME 19 lines; a test
# (scripts/ci/test_win_vm_vast.py) fails if the two lists differ. `run` logs this file's name, sha256 prefix and flag
# count (ENV_FILE) and the resulting KF3_* environment (KF3_ENV).
KF3_WIN_USER_CHANNELS_PASSTHROUGH=1
KF3_WIN_TWIN_DEFAPI_OBJECT=1
KF3_KERNEL_GR_CE=1
KF3_KERNEL_GR_WORK=1
KF3_TRANSLATED_CE_RELAY=1
KF3_DEFERRED_API=1
KF3_PREEMPT_BIND_PROBE=1
KF3_DISPLAY_IMP_ENABLE=1
KF3_DISPLAY_CTRL_PROBE=1
KF3_ZCULL_BIND_PROBE=1
KF3_SW_RUNLIST_HOST_OWNED=1
KF3_ASYNC_PREEMPT=1
KF3_GFX_POOL_PROBE=1
KF3_SW_RUNLIST_PROBE=1
KF3_MEMORY_LIST_PROBE=1
KF3_DISPLAY_SDR_COLOR=1
KF3_DISPLAY_CAPS_PROBE=1
KF3_DISPLAY_LUT_MIRROR=1
KF3_DISPLAY_ILUT_OFFSET_256=1
